Hi Andy,

Thanks for the thorough and clear explanation of what you're hitting.  I suspect the problem is in this line:

X[i,t,c] ~ dnorm(G[c,i] + delta[c,1,i]*w[1,t] + delta[c,2,i]*w[2,t] + rho.x[c]*(X[i,(t-1),c] - (G[c,i] + delta[c,1]*w[1,(t-1),i] + delta[c,2]*w[2,(t-1),i])), tau = tau.x[c])

I see here, in the last two terms of the mean, delta with 2 indices and w with 3 indices.  I am wondering if it is possible that you meant to insert the third index, 'i', into the delta's rather than the w's?

-Perry

